---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | PubMed Trivia"
  description="Terms of Use for PubMed Trivia, covering acceptable use, copyright, and disclaimers."
  lang="en"
>
  <article>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>

    <p>
      These Terms of Use govern your access to and use of PubMed Trivia (the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;).
      By visiting or using this Site, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree,
      please do not use this Site.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Purpose of the Site</h2>
    <p>
      PubMed Trivia summarizes and reviews peer-reviewed research &mdash; especially
      systematic reviews and meta-analyses &mdash; indexed in the U.S. National Library
      of Medicine&rsquo;s PubMed database, in the fields of biology, medicine, and psychology.
      The Site is an educational and informational outlet, not a medical practice or clinical
      service.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Not Medical Advice</h2>
    <p>
      Content on this Site is <strong>not a substitute for professional medical advice,
      diagnosis, or treatment</strong>. Always seek the advice of a qualified health
      professional (physician, pharmacist, nurse, or equivalent) for questions about a
      medical condition. PubMed Trivia and its editors assume no liability for actions
      taken based on information found on this Site.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Copyright, citation, and reuse</h2>
    <p>
      Article text, images, logos, and design elements on this Site are the property of the
      PubMed Trivia editorial team or its licensors. You may quote the Site under the
      following conditions without prior permission:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The quotation is relevant to and necessary for your own content.</li>
      <li>The quoted portion is clearly secondary to your own writing.</li>
      <li>The quoted portion is clearly distinguishable from your own text.</li>
      <li>You attribute the source with the URL and the site name &ldquo;PubMed Trivia&rdquo;.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For wholesale reproduction, translation, or substantially modified reuse, please
      contact us via the <a href="/en/contact/">Contact page</a> first.
    </p>
    <p>
      Copyright in the original PubMed-indexed articles belongs to the respective authors
      and publishers. PubMed Trivia does not reproduce full article text; we provide original
      summaries and commentary based on publicly available abstracts. For the full paper,
      please consult PubMed directly.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Prohibited uses</h2>
    <p>
      You must not do any of the following while using this Site:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Impose an unreasonable load on our servers or network, including large-scale
          automated scraping or crawling that disregards robots directives.</li>
      <li>Reproduce, redistribute, or commercially exploit Site content without permission.</li>
      <li>Present information from this Site to others as personalized medical advice.</li>
      <li>Harass, defame, or threaten the editors, operators, or other users of the Site.</li>
      <li>Interfere with the Site&rsquo;s operation in any manner.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      We make reasonable efforts to ensure accuracy, completeness, and timeliness, but do not
      warrant any of these. To the fullest extent permitted by law, PubMed Trivia disclaims
      liability for any direct or indirect damages arising from reliance on Site content.
    </p>
    <p>
      External links from this Site (to PubMed, Amazon, Rakuten Books, and others) are
      provided for convenience only. We are not responsible for the content, terms, or
      privacy practices of those external sites. Please review their terms separately.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Advertising, affiliate, and personal data</h2>
    <p>
      This Site participates in advertising and affiliate programs. See our
      <a href="/en/disclosure/">Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure</a> and
      <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms at any time. The current version applies from the moment it is
      posted on this page. For material changes, we will note the update date and a brief
      summary of what changed.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of Japan. Any disputes arising from the use of
      this Site shall be submitted to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Tokyo District Court
      as the court of first instance.
    </p>

    <p>
      <small>Last updated: 18 November 2026</small>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
